WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:09.969
If rules exist, we’ll find a way around
them… and even Pokemon Go is no exception.

00:00:09.969 --> 00:00:14.059
Players everywhere have found ways to bend—or
break—the game's rules.

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:18.720
Some of these methods are fairly harmless,
while others can get you banned.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:24.400
Here's how to cheat in Pokemon Go—but don't
say we didn't warn you...

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.060
Egg-hatching machines

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:31.140
Are you too tired or lazy to walk around and
hatch those eggs you've had forever?

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:35.570
No problem—just use something else to do
it for you!

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:40.360
Creative Pokemon Go players have come up with
all sorts of ways to hatch their eggs without

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.640
also working their glutes.

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.980
Some trainers have even started strapping
their phones to their actual, real-life pets

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:50.940
before sending them outside to play.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:56.120
Others use spinning household objects like
turntables, bicycle wheels, and even ceiling

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.540
fans to do the work.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:01.670
Of course, don't use the spinning plate in
your microwave for this method.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:07.420
Despite the memes floating around showing
a phone safely spinning inside a microwave,

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:12.930
if you do this, all you'll end up with is
a broken warranty, some dead Pikachus, and

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.930
a very disappointed dad.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:16.069
Stealing gyms

00:01:16.069 --> 00:01:21.049
After a Gym attack brings its prestige down
to zero, it becomes neutral until a player

00:01:21.049 --> 00:01:24.200
places a new Pokemon in as a defender.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:30.180
That may take a few moments, because players
can only use fully-healed Pokemon as defenders.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:34.840
If you don't have creatures that are strong
enough to take over a Gym yet, those few seconds

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.430
are your opportunity.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:42.720
Watch for the Gym to turn neutral, then immediately
tap on it and place one of your Pokemon in

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:43.720
there as a defender.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:49.560
Next, go to your Shop menu and tap the shield
icon to claim your daily defender bonus of

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.229
Pokecoins and Stardust.

00:01:51.229 --> 00:01:55.110
You'll claim a Gym without having to attack
even once.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:59.020
Who needs friends when you have imaginary
dust?

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:01.399
Pick your Eevee-lution

00:02:01.399 --> 00:02:06.619
When you evolve an Eevee in Pokemon Go, it
can turn into one of three different forms,

00:02:06.619 --> 00:02:07.789
seemingly at random.

00:02:07.789 --> 00:02:12.670
If you want some control, however, name them
after the original Eevee trainers from the

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:14.190
Pokemon cartoon.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:19.780
Naming your Eevee "Sparky" will net you a
Jolteon; "Rainer" will get you a Vaporeon;

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:22.080
and "Pyro" will result in a Flareon.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.940
You may need to restart your app after naming
your Eevee before proceeding with the evolution

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:27.940
process.

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:31.800
And remember: you can always change those
dorky names to something way cooler later.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:32.930
GPS spoofing

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:39.920
Put simply, GPS spoofing is making your device
pretend to be at a location that you are not.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:44.940
Some trainers, like popular YouTuber PewDiePie,
have gone to some extreme lengths to do this,

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:49.770
like strapping their phone to a remote-controlled
drone and flying it around while playing the

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.190
game via their laptop at home.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:57.500
Technologically savvy cheaters can also install
a program called Bluestacks on their computer,

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:03.090
which creates a virtual Android environment
on the PC that acts just like a phone.

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:07.570
After rooting the device, they can install
a modified version of Pokemon Go, as well

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:09.710
as a GPS faking app.

00:03:09.710 --> 00:03:14.890
Once everything is set up, cheaters can set
their "location" via the fake GPS app on the

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:19.620
device, open up Pokemon Go, and then play
the game without leaving home.

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:23.030
If you want to know more, you’re probably
a bad person.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:27.610
Early reports indicate that most cheaters
who are being found out are only being given

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:31.340
a soft ban, locking them out of the game for
an hour or two at the most.

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:35.060
But there are also more and more reports of
permanent bans.

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:39.560
So, play fair, or get kicked out of Pokemon
for all eternity.

00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:44.170
“Why don’t those stupid idiots let me
in their crappy club for jerks?”

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:45.170
Thanks for watching!

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:49.170
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:52.740
And leave us a comment to let us know what
you think of Pokemon Go cheaters…

